From 4992d9cc5968ccf052276272a48cd577332720ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:11:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] openwrt: rebase the netifd multicast_wakeupcall bit onto
 OpenWrt main

The netifd patch inside Gluon's MLD querier wake-up patch gives
DEV_OPT_MULTICAST_WAKEUPCALL bit 63, the far end of what used to be a
hand-numbered enum. The netifd on OpenWrt main derives every DEV_OPT_
flag as "1ULL << DEV_ATTR_<name>", and bit 63 now belongs to
DEV_OPT_DEFAULT_MACADDR. The hunk no longer applies, and applied with
fuzz it would alias the two flags.

Derive the flag the same way as its neighbours. The DEV_ATTR_ hunk is
unchanged and still puts DEV_ATTR_MULTICAST_WAKEUPCALL next to
DEV_ATTR_MULTICAST_TO_UNICAST, among the options that need a teardown to
be re-applied, which is where a bridge multicast option belongs.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
---
 ...wake-up-calls-Android-bug-workaround.patch | 24 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/patches/openwrt/0002-kernel-bridge-Implement-MLD-Querier-wake-up-calls-Android-bug-workaround.patch b/patches/openwrt/0002-kernel-bridge-Implement-MLD-Querier-wake-up-calls-Android-bug-workaround.patch
index db17ed16..1f553353 100644
